      {
        "lesson_index": 3,
        "lesson_title": "Laplace Transform of $e^{-at}u(t)$",
        "section_index": 3,
        "section_title": "Evaluating the Integral to Obtain $1/(s+a)$",
        "step_type": "example",
        "question_type": "multiple-choice",
        "answer_cardinality": "single",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "question_count": 2,
        "questions": [
          {
            "question_index": 1,
            "question_type": "multiple-choice",
            "answer_cardinality": "single",
            "prompt_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Evaluate $\\mathcal{L}_+\\{e^{-4t}u(t)\\}$ from the one-sided integral and simplify the result.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ],
            "choices": [
              {
                "choice_label": "A",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$\\frac{1}{s+4}$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": true
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "B",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$\\frac{1}{s-4}$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "C",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$\\frac{1}{4-s}$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "D",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$\\operatorname{Re}(s)>-4$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "E",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$\\frac{1}{s+4}+C$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              }
            ],
            "correct_choice_labels": [
              "A"
            ],
            "correct_answer": "$\\frac{1}{s+4}$",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "The one-sided integral is $\\int_{0^-}^{\\infty} e^{-(s+4)t}\\,dt$. The antiderivative is $-\\frac{1}{s+4}e^{-(s+4)t}$, and with $\\operatorname{Re}(s)>-4$, the upper-limit term is $0$, leaving $\\frac{1}{s+4}$.",
